# RTL (700) - SystemVerilog conventions

Thin Must / Must-not glob for FPGA DUT; no CPU ISA inventory. Recipes: `.cursor/skills/sc-rtl/references/core.md`. This glob does not require Yosys/nextpnr as the only legal flow.

## Must

- Every `.sv`: open with `` `default_nettype none ``, close with `` `default_nettype wire ``
- Sync reset inside RTL; default active-high `rst`; convert board active-low at boundary (FPGA default: synchronous reset)
- Sequential: `always_ff @(posedge clk)` with `if (rst)` inside the block
- Reset **control** bits (`valid`/`pending`), not payload-only regs
- Prefer `case` / `unique case` for mutually exclusive FSM/decode; nested `if` only when priority is real
- no latches; full assign in `always_comb` / every branch
- `snake_case`; purpose prefixes (`imem_`, `dmem_`); keep RISC-V port names
- Register at natural boundaries for Fmax; multi-cycle stage large cones; document unregistered exemptions (handshake `*_ready` OK)
- Lint before claim: Verilator `--lint-only` (or project lint/synth target) is build-breaking unless waived with rationale

## Must not

- Async reset inside project RTL modules (FPGA default: sync)
- Blocking (`=`) in sequential `always_ff` for flops (`sim≠synth`)
- Combinational loops; multi-driven nets; undriven outputs left silent
- Blind "fix all" lint without disposition (fix / waive-system / monitor) - see `sc-rtl`

## Project SPEC wins

ISA subset, memory map, FPGA target, and paths come from mission `spec.md` / `docs/SPECIFICATION.md` when present.
